                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72917c41-bb04-3563-912c-57302f473c8b",
                        "entry_id": "299ccf36-a611-3ad5-8b53-c0595ab0970b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rejeter ou retirer d'un texte un passage considéré comme douteux ou apocryphe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a230b9e-44ea-46a4-8646-d2e22e41412b",
                                "sense_id": "72917c41-bb04-3563-912c-57302f473c8b",
                                "text": "C'est pourquoi Barigazzi athétise, en plus de la ligne répétée προσφερομένου ... σελήνην, les mots ἀποφέρομενων ἀτόμων, qui pourraient, selon lui, représenter les restes d'une glose, jadis inscrite en marge de la première."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3bf2f988-cd20-4f4e-8fe7-a433c36e44f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "299ccf36-a611-3ad5-8b53-c0595ab0970b",
                        "source_sense_id": "72917c41-bb04-3563-912c-57302f473c8b",
                        "target_lang_word": "athetize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "athetize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "557798e8-0628-3d08-b1d6-c9936681cc09",
                                        "entry_id": "a6decb20-fb16-383e-97a7-769fc136049b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To reject a passage of text as spurious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "English",
                                            "Oxford",
                                            "US",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "094523d2-33ef-47d0-8395-468ba71c1d3e",
                                                "sense_id": "557798e8-0628-3d08-b1d6-c9936681cc09",
                                                "text": "But this is a doubtful compliment to a ship ; the alternative \"a first-rate sailor,\" suits the context better, and so here, \"or first-rate build,\" primarie compacti (Döderl[ein]), avoids the awkward tautology with νεοτευχέες which made Zenod[otos] athetize the line."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1058158f-7ac1-411a-a90f-430adec25a6a",
                                                "sense_id": "557798e8-0628-3d08-b1d6-c9936681cc09",
                                                "text": "All of this, of course, flies in the face of μιχτὴν ϱ̔αψῳδίαων. But that phrase is suspicious in its own right. It was bracketed long ago by Tyrwhitt, and the Arabic version translates it strangely if at all. […] In short, there is every reason to athetize μιχτὴν ραψῳδίαων as a note of late origin which has gotten into the text."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
